## 5. Optional Jira write

**AskQuestion:** write **Story Point estimate** / skip.

If **confidence is 0–2**, say in the prompt that the estimate is low accuracy (the number is still the raw Fibonacci Estimate) before the user chooses write or skip. Do **not** put that warning on the Jira issue.

On write:

1. **`getJiraIssue`** for the confirmed key (read current **labels** and any existing Story Point estimate).
2. **`editJiraIssue`** — set **Story Point estimate** to the **confirmed Fibonacci Estimate** (raw). Never a confidence-adjusted number. Field display name; resolve custom field id from the issue if the API rejects display name only.
3. **Labels (hard rule):**
   - **Never delete a label that does not start with `y-ai-`.** Copy every such label through unchanged (`pmroo`, `command-center`, etc.).
   - **Only modify `y-ai-*` labels this rule owns.** Do not remove other `y-ai-*` labels from a different workflow.
   - When the API requires a full labels array, **read current labels first**, then send the **merged** list. Never send only the new `y-ai-*` labels.
   - Add **`y-ai-estimated`** if not already present.
   - Set **`y-ai-est-confidence-<n>`** — `n` is the confirmed integer **0–5** (examples: `y-ai-est-confidence-3`, `y-ai-est-confidence-5`). Remove only previous **confidence** labels this rule uses (`y-ai-est-confidence-0` … `y-ai-est-confidence-5`, plus legacy `y-ai-est-confidence-0/5` … `y-ai-est-confidence-5/5`, `y-ai-est-confident-0` … `y-ai-est-confident-5`, and `y-ai-confidence-0/5` … `y-ai-confidence-5/5`) so one current score remains.
   - Add **`y-ai-needs-refinement`** when confidence is **0–2** or when the recommendation is `/y-team-task-refinement`. On a later write, **remove that same label** if confidence is 3–5 and refinement is no longer recommended.
   - Do **not** add `y-ai-needs-refinement` only because the ticket is large and we recommend split.

Confirm before write. After success, tell the user the points, **`y-ai-estimated`**, **`y-ai-est-confidence-<n>`**, and **`y-ai-needs-refinement`** if it was added or removed.

If MCP fails, paste the number and ask the user to set Story Point estimate and add labels **`y-ai-estimated`** and **`y-ai-est-confidence-<n>`** (and **`y-ai-needs-refinement`** when it applies) manually — without deleting other labels.

Do **not** write Jira without this gate. Do **not** add these labels when the user skips the Jira write.

Do **not** add Jira comments, description edits, or warning / buffer wording on the issue.

---

## One ticket per run

Do not estimate a whole sprint or epic as one number — still give **one Fibonacci number** for the item you were asked to estimate; **recommend** child items / split beside it.

